{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts | sed -n '24,42p'\"","aggregated_output":"    24\t} from \"./types.js\";\n    25\t\n    26\t// DD-7: a pathological tool result must not blow a small-context model.\n    27\t// Content over the bound keeps its head and tail around a marker, and the\n    28\t// bounded whole stays within maxInputChars; bounding happens before prompt\n    29\t// rendering, so the dropped middle never crosses the boundary.\n    30\tfunction boundContent(content: string, maxInputChars: number): string {\n    31\t  if (content.length <= maxInputChars) return content;\n    32\t  const marker = `\\n\\n[... truncated: tool result was ${String(content.length)} chars; head and tail retained ...]\\n\\n`;\n    33\t  const keep = Math.max(0, maxInputChars - marker.length);\n    34\t  const head = Math.ceil(keep / 2);\n    35\t  const tail = keep - head;\n    36\t  return content.slice(0, head) + marker + (tail > 0 ? content.slice(content.length - tail) : \"\");\n    37\t}\n    38\t\n    39\t// Failure mapping (DD-3): the queue consumes `retryable` exactly as it always\n    40\t// has, and the reason string is machine-readable by the established\n    41\t// code-before-first-colon convention. Retryable failures lead with\n    42\t// `provider_failure` — the code Epic 02 has always landed on exhausted forms\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
