{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md | sed -n '43,54p;156,178p'\"","aggregated_output":"    43\t  - brief-summary rendering contains outcome tokens but no receipt text from its input\n    44\t  - oversized `summarizeToolResult` input renders head + tail + marker under `maxInputChars`; under-limit input renders whole\n    45\t- **TC-2.3** (AC-2.4): `inference-adapter.test.ts`\n    46\t  - fake function returns `{ ok: true, text: \"  \" }`, then success; first attempt classifies `empty_output` retryable and retry lands `ready`\n    47\t  - all-whitespace script exhausts budget; form lands `failed` with reason `provider_failure` and last error naming `empty_output`\n    48\t\n    49\t### Technical Design\n    50\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n    51\t\n    52\t#### Architecture Context\n    53\t\n    54\tThis story builds the semantic inference layer behind the unchanged Epic 02 provider seam. The adapter implements `DerivationProvider`, renders LHC-owned prompt templates, calls the host `ModelCall`, shapes successful text, and returns config-stamped provenance.\n   156\t3. Call the host `ModelCall` with the kind's provider/model assignment.\n   157\t4. Treat empty or whitespace-only success text as `empty_output`.\n   158\t5. Return shaped text plus config-known provenance.\n   159\t\n   160\tThe adapter never parses model text for outcomes, receipts, or mechanical facts. Those remain handler-authored from the record.\n   161\t\n   162\t#### Source/Derived State Risk\n   163\t\n   164\t- Source facts stay in record-owned handlers.\n   165\t- Provider text is derived content only.\n   166\t- `DerivedFormMetadata.provenance` is copied from the provider result, which is stamped by the adapter from config-known strings.\n   167\t\n   168\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\n   169\t\n   170\t- Do not satisfy tests by calling prompt renderers directly without exercising the adapter operation.\n   171\t- Do not parse output text for facts, receipts, or provenance.\n   172\t- Do not create prompt placeholders without golden coverage.\n   173\t- Do not let an empty string land as `ready`.\n   174\t\n   175\t#### Production Path Proof\n   176\t\n   177\t- Entrypoint: domain handlers call the configured `DerivationProvider` operations during drain.\n   178\t- Registration/default path: Story 2 constructs the adapter into the SDK provider slot; this story implements the adapter behind that slot.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
