\n- Epic 04 builds the inspection surface for the LHC SDK (in-process long-horizon-context system for PI CLI extensions; thin CLI for testing/integration).\\\\n- S1 message reads: listMessages bounds {from,to,limit,includeDeleted} in source-event order; show returns FULL record blocks + owner-reported form states (never view-shortened, never synthesized); deleted excluded by default, auditable, show on deleted = ok+flag, missing id = message_not_found; CLI deep-equal parity. Search deferred post-v1, no placeholder. Strategy: simple-risk-reminders.\\\\n- S2 inspect domain: overview (identity, event/message/turn/chunk counts, derivation states, view summary or null, boundary + zone tokens; deleted contract; all 5 thread shapes; pure read) + health (owner/kind/state counts via owner report surfaces ONLY — no direct derived_form/work_item reads; failure detail; repair preview = failed∧¬blocked, never executed; queue visibility; rebuild bracket edit→pending→drain→ready). Read-only delta helper lands here, wraps S1 ops retroactively. Mutation-in-flight fixture via production mutate + partial drain, never hand-written rows. Strategy: tdd-lite.\\\\n- S3 view report: threadView.describe = stored snapshot only (null when absent, never recompute); inspect.view = describe + measured pull tail; governing contract loadCost.total == actual pull served content (incl. never-compacted: meta null, bands [], tail-only). No new storage/migration. Strategy: tdd-lite.\\\\n- S4 lifecycle capstone: test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts scripted PI-extension order (create→intake→drain→status→compact→pull→inspect→edit+delete→rebuild drain→health→compact2→pull→materialize); deterministic provider only, zero network; replay byte-identical; SDK teardown/recreate continuity; spawned-CLI checkpoint parity; receipt-vs-health cross-check. Process suite must report ran, never silently skip. Strategy: full-staged-risk.\\\\n- Test plan: ~26 default tests across messages-read/inspect-overview/inspect-view/inspect-health/lifecycle + cli-process-inspect (process: TC-3.4, TC-5.4). Architecture-risk: read-only delta assert on every new op; throwing-provider suite-wide assert; loadCost parity two independent measurements; check-boundaries + source check against raw SQL into other domains from domains/inspect/**.\\\\n\\\\n## Operating Reminders\\\\n\\\\n- Impl-lead owns acceptance, final gates, fix routing, recovery. CLI never accepts.\\\\n- Story cycle: story-orchestrate validate → run (background) → monitor via runtime progress artifacts + 5-min Monitor cadence → review final package → run story gate myself → receipt → advance.\\\\n- Receipt before acceptance: implementor evidence, verifier evidence, gate result, dispositions, baseline before/after.\\\\n- Cumulative baseline tracking: total test count must not regress story-over-story.\\\\n\\\\n## Cumulative Baseline\\\\n\\\\n- Pre-run baseline (2026-06-12, before Story 1): `pnpm verify` PASS — 290 tests / 27 files.\\\\n\\\\n## Story Sequence Status\\\\n\\\\n| Story | Status |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| 01-message-read-surface | pending |\\\\n| 02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health | pending |\\\\n| 03-view-contents-report | pending |\\\\n| 04-lifecycle-exercise | pending |\\\\n\\\\n## Transitions\\\\n\\\\n- 2026-06-12: Run created. State: SETUP. inspect ready; config authored; gates resolved from package scripts.\\\\n- 2026-06-12: preflight ready (002-preflight.json). Gates persisted into impl-run.config.json by preflight (expected side effect). Baseline 290/27 recorded. State → STORY_ACTIVE, Story 01, phase implement.\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":64,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":64}}}\\n118:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01WVsp1svp4RxDnvsFfwcj3y\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t# Story 1: Message Read Surface\\\\n2\\\\t\\\\n3\\\\t### Summary\\\\n4\\\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\\\n5\\\\tComplete message listing and single-message viewing with deleted-audit support and CLI parity.\\\\n6\\\\t\\\\n7\\\\t### Description\\\\n8\\\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\\\n9\\\\t**User Profile:** The operator audits threads from the CLI; agents inside a harness use the same reads mid-task.\\\\n10\\\\t\\\\n11\\\\t**Objective:** Provide the drill-down floor for every report that names message subjects.\\\\n12\\\\t\\\\n13\\\\t**Scope In:** `messages.list` bounded listing options, `messages.show`, forms join, deleted-message audit option, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`, SDK/CLI JSON parity.\\\\n14\\\\t\\\\n15\\\\t**Scope Out:** Message search is deferred post-v1. No search behavior, search placeholder, ranking, FTS, or result-granularity decision ships in this story.\\\\n16\\\\t\\\\n17\\\\t**Dependencies:** Built Epic 01 message record/read-back behavior and Epic 02 report/deleted-message contracts.\\\\n18\\\\t\\\\n19\\\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n20\\\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\\\n21\\\\t- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\\\\n22\\\\t\\\\n23\\\\t- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\\\\n24\\\\t\\\\n25\\\\t- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\\\\n26\\\\t\\\\n27\\\\t- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\\\\n28\\\\t\\\\n29\\\\t- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\\\\n30\\\\t\\\\n31\\\\t- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\\\\n32\\\\t\\\\n33\\\\t- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\\\\n34\\\\t\\\\n35\\\\t- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\\\\n36\\\\t\\\\n37\\\\t### Technical Design\\\\n38\\\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\\\n39\\\\t#### Architecture Context\\\\n40\\\\t\\\\n41\\\\tThis story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\\\\n42\\\\t\\\\n43\\\\tThe CLI is a thin argv-to-SDK wrapper. JSON output must deep-equal the in-process SDK result.\\\\n44\\\\t\\\\n45\\\\t#### Build Strategy\\\\n46\\\\t\\\\n47\\\\tStrategy: simple-risk-reminders\\\\n48\\\\t\\\\n49\\\\tReason:\\\\n50\\\\t- One surface owns listing/showing behavior, but bounds semantics, deleted defaults, and CLI parity are easy to shortcut.\\\\n51\\\\t\\\\n52\\\\tRisk Reminders:\\\\n53\\\\t- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\\\\n54\\\\t- Deleted messages remain excluded by default and auditable on explicit request.\\\\n55\\\\t- Bounds use source-event-order coordinates: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`.\\\\n56\\\\t\\\\n57\\\\t#### Implementation Targets\\\\n58\\\\t\\\\n59\\\\t| Area | Files / Modules |\\\\n60\\\\t|------|-----------------|\\\\n61\\\\t| Message surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` |\\\\n62\\\\t| CLI | `src/cli/messages-read.ts` |\\\\n63\\\\t| SDK export | `src/sdk.ts` |\\\\n64\\\\t| Tests | `test/messages-read.test.ts`, `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` |\\\\n65\\\\t\\\\n66\\\\t#### Design References\\\\n67\\\\t\\\\n68\\\\t- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\\\\n69\\\\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 3: Message Listing and Show](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:139), lines 139-142\\\\n70\\\\t- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:189), lines 189-213\\\\n71\\\\t- [test-plan.md §Test Files](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:6), lines 6-18\\\\n72\\\\t- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\\\n73\\\\t- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\\\\n74\\\\t\\\\n75\\\\t#### Test Mapping\\\\n76\\\\t\\\\n77\\\\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\\\n78\\\\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\\\\n79\\\\t| TC-3.1 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: order, fields, bounds` | Record order, kind, token estimate, turn id, exact `from`/`to`/`limit` windows, and bad bounds error. |\\\\n80\\\\t| TC-3.2 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: show full record + forms` | Drained tool-result message returns full content, form states, and outcome metadata. |\\\\n81\\\\t| TC-3.3 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: deleted handling` | Default list excludes deleted; include-deleted marks it; show on deleted returns ok with flag; missing id returns not found. |\\\\n82\\\\t| TC-3.4 | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts :: list/show parity` | Spawned CLI message list/show JSON deep-equals SDK results. |\\\\n83\\\\t\\\\n84\\\\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\\\n85\\\\t\\\\n86\\\\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\\\n87\\\\t|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\\\n88\\\\t| Read-only drift | `test/messages-read.test.ts` read-only legs | Before/after observable-state snapshots stay equal for list/show. | A read can satisfy shape assertions while still mutating queue, boundary, or view state. |\\\\n89\\\\t| CLI bypasses SDK | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` process parity | Spawned commands compare serialized JSON against SDK results. | Private helper tests can pass while production CLI output diverges. |\\\\n90\\\\t\\\\n91\\\\t#### Technical Notes\\\\n92\\\\t\\\\n93\\\\t- `listMessages` option defaults must preserve existing callers: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\\\\n94\\\\t- `from` and `to` are source-event-order bounds; `limit` caps after bounds.\\\\n95\\\\t- `show` composes the by-id message read with `messages.report(ref, { messageId })`.\\\\n96\\\\t- Message search remains deferred post-v1 and gets no v1 placeholder behavior.\\\\n97\\\\t\\\\n98\\\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\\\n99\\\\t\\\\n100\\\\t- Assert real full block content for tool-result messages, not only message id or metadata.\\\\n101\\\\t- Exercise the spawned `lhc messages` commands for process parity.\\\\n102\\\\t- Do not synthesize form state in `show`; use the owner report entries.\\\\n103\\\\t\\\\n104\\\\t#### Production Path Proof\\\\n105\\\\t\\\\n106\\\\t- Entrypoint: `messages.listMessages`, `messages.show`, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`.\\\\n107\\\\t- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes the message operations; `src/cli/messages-read.ts` routes CLI commands to SDK calls.\\\\n108\\\\t- Evidence: process parity for CLI list/show and default-suite message read tests.\\\\n109\\\\t\\\\n110\\\\t#### Verification\\\\n111\\\\t\\\\n112\\\\t- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\\\n113\\\\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\\\n114\\\\t- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\\\n115\\\\t\\\\n116\\\\t#### Spec Deviations\\\\n117\\\\t\\\\n118\\\\tNone.\\\\n119\\\\t\\\\n120\\\\t### Definition of Done\\\\n121\\\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\\\n122\\\\t- `messages.list` returns bounded, ordered message summaries with deleted filtering.\\\\n123\\\\t- `messages.show` returns full record content and owner-reported form state for one message.\\\\n124\\\\t- Deleted-message audit behavior matches Epic 02's deleted contract.\\\\n125\\\\t- CLI list/show options and JSON match SDK results.\\\\n126\\\\t- TC-3.1 through TC-3.4 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\\\n127\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"f853556b-5c91-4adf-871d-8a3cc45d9e24\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T13:24:17.982Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Story 1: Message Read Surface\\\\n\\\\n### Summary\\\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\\\nComplete message listing and single-message viewing with deleted-audit support and CLI parity.\\\\n\\\\n### Description\\\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\\\n**User Profile:** The operator audits threads from the CLI; agents inside a harness use the same reads mid-task.\\\\n\\\\n**Objective:** Provide the drill-down floor for every report that names message subjects.\\\\n\\\\n**Scope In:** `messages.list` bounded listing options, `messages.show`, forms join, deleted-message audit option, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`, SDK/CLI JSON parity.\\\\n\\\\n**Scope Out:** Message search is deferred post-v1. No search behavior, search placeholder, ranking, FTS, or result-granularity decision ships in this story.\\\\n\\\\n**Dependencies:** Built Epic 01 message record/read-back behavior and Epic 02 report/deleted-message contracts.\\\\n\\\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\\\n- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\\\\n\\\\n### Technical Design\\\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\\\n#### Architecture Context\\\\n\\\\nThis story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\\\\n\\\\nThe CLI is a thin argv-to-SDK wrapper. JSON output must deep-equal the in-process SDK result.\\\\n\\\\n#### Build Strategy\\\\n\\\\nStrategy: simple-risk-reminders\\\\n\\\\nReason:\\\\n- One surface owns listing/showing behavior, but bounds semantics, deleted defaults, and CLI parity are easy to shortcut.\\\\n\\\\nRisk Reminders:\\\\n- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\\\\n- Deleted messages remain excluded by default and auditable on explicit request.\\\\n- Bounds use source-event-order coordinates: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Implementation Targets\\\\n\\\\n| Area | Files / Modules |\\\\n|------|-----------------|\\\\n| Message surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` |\\\\n| CLI | `src/cli/messages-read.ts` |\\\\n| SDK export | `src/sdk.ts` |\\\\n| Tests | `test/messages-read.test.ts`, `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` |\\\\n\\\\n#### Design References\\\\n\\\\n- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\\\\n- [tech-design.md §Flow 3: Message Listing and Show](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:139), lines 139-142\\\\n- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:189), lines 189-213\\\\n- [test-plan.md §Test Files](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:6), lines 6-18\\\\n- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\\\n- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\\\\n\\\\n#### Test Mapping\\\\n\\\\n| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\\\n|----|-------------------|------------------|\\\\n| TC-3.1 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: order, fields, bounds` | Record order, kind, token estimate, turn id, exact `from`/`to`/`limit` windows, and bad bounds error. |\\\\n| TC-3.2 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: show full record + forms` | Drained tool-result message returns full content, form states, and outcome metadata. |\\\\n| TC-3.3 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: deleted handling` | Default list excludes deleted; include-deleted marks it; show on deleted returns ok with flag; missing id returns not found. |\\\\n| TC-3.4 | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts :: list/show parity` | Spawned CLI message list/show JSON deep-equals SDK results. |\\\\n\\\\n#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\\\n\\\\n| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\\\n|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\\\n| Read-only drift | `test/messages-read.test.ts` read-only legs | Before/after observable-state snapshots stay equal for list/show. | A read can satisfy shape assertions while still mutating queue, boundary, or view state. |\\\\n| CLI bypasses SDK | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` process parity | Spawned commands compare serialized JSON against SDK results. | Private helper tests can pass while production CLI output diverges. |\\\\n\\\\n#### Technical Notes\\\\n\\\\n- `listMessages` option defaults must preserve existing callers: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\\\\n- `from` and `to` are source-event-order bounds; `limit` caps after bounds.\\\\n- `show` composes the by-id message read with `messages.report(ref, { messageId })`.\\\\n- Message search remains deferred post-v1 and gets no v1 placeholder behavior.\\\\n\\\\n#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\\\n\\\\n- Assert real full block content for tool-result messages, not only message id or metadata.\\\\n- Exercise the spawned `lhc messages` commands for process parity.\\\\n- Do not synthesize form state in `show`; use the owner report entries.\\\\n\\\\n#### Production Path Proof\\\\n\\\\n- Entrypoint: `messages.listMessages`, `messages.show`, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`.\\\\n- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes the message operations; `src/cli/messages-read.ts` routes CLI commands to SDK calls.\\\\n- Evidence: process parity for CLI list/show and default-suite message read tests.\\\\n\\\\n#### Verification\\\\n\\\\n- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\\\n- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\\\n- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\\\n\\\\n#### Spec Deviations\\\\n\\\\nNone.\\\\n\\\\n### Definition of Done\\\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\\\n- `messages.list` returns bounded, ordered message summaries with deleted filtering.\\\\n- `messages.show` returns full record content and owner-reported form state for one message.\\\\n- Deleted-message audit behavior matches Epic 02's deleted contract.\\\\n- CLI list/show options and JSON match SDK results.\\\\n- TC-3.1 through TC-3.4 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":127,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":127}}}\\n127:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01SJ8QEoT3GKMUnb9R7yNS8o\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t// Story 1 (Epic 04), default suite: TC-3.1–3.3 — the message read surface.\\\\n2\\\\t// Bounded listing in source-event-order coordinates (DD-3), show returning\\\\n3\\\\t// the canonical record (full blocks, never view-shortened) composed with the\\\\n4\\\\t// owner report's form entries (DD-2), and the deleted-audit contract\\\\n5\\\\t// (excluded by default, listable flagged on request, show never not-found).\\\\n6\\\\t// Plus the architecture-risk legs: every read leaves observable state\\\\n7\\\\t// unchanged (read-only delta, DD-6) and calls no provider.\\\\n8\\\\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\\\\\"vitest\\\\\\\";\\\\n9\\\\timport {\\\\n10\\\\t  createSdk,\\\\n11\\\\t  intakeStream,\\\\n12\\\\t  messages,\\\\n13\\\\t  threadView,\\\\n14\\\\t  turns,\\\\n15\\\\t  type Lhc,\\\\n16\\\\t  type MessageEventInput,\\\\n17\\\\t} from \\\\\\\"../src/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n18\\\\timport {\\\\n19\\\\t  createProviderDouble,\\\\n20\\\\t  openRaw,\\\\n21\\\\t  poisonMessageBlockJson,\\\\n22\\\\t  poisonMessageFormJson,\\\\n23\\\\t  readDerivedForms,\\\\n24\\\\t  tempStore,\\\\n25\\\\t  validEvent,\\\\n26\\\\t  type TempStore,\\\\n27\\\\t} from \\\\\\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n28\\\\t\\\\n29\\\\t// Long enough that any view-form shortening would be visible: show must\\\\n30\\\\t// return this verbatim (AC-3.2's record-not-view contract).\\\\n31\\\\tconst TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT = [\\\\n32\\\\t  \\\\\\\"contents of notes.txt — full record content:\\\\\\\",\\\\n33\\\\t  \\\\\\\"line 1: the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\\\\\\\",\\\\n34\\\\t  \\\\\\\"line 2: detailed tool output that a boundary-shortened form would drop\\\\\\\",\\\\n35\\\\t  \\\\\\\"line 3: trailing detail proving the record came back complete\\\\\\\",\\\\n36\\\\t].join(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\");\\\\n37\\\\t\\\\n38\\\\tinterface ReadFixture {\\\\n39\\\\t  filePath: string;\\\\n40\\\\t  sdk: Lhc;\\\\n41\\\\t  double: ReturnType<typeof createProviderDouble>;\\\\n42\\\\t}\\\\n43\\\\t\\\\n44\\\\t// Two closed turns through real intake, fully drained against the\\\\n45\\\\t// deterministic double so m1's smoothing and m3/m4's tool summaries sit\\\\n46\\\\t// ready with mechanically stamped outcome metadata. Messages: m1 prompt,\\\\n47\\\\t// m2 text, m3 call, m4 result (turn 1; turn_end is event 5, no message);\\\\n48\\\\t// m6 prompt, m7 text (turn 2). Source event orders 1,2,3,4,6,7.\\\\n49\\\\tasync function readFixture(store: TempStore): Promise<ReadFixture> {\\\\n50\\\\t  const double = createProviderDouble();\\\\n51\\\\t  const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\" });\\\\n52\\\\t  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\\\n53\\\\t  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({\\\\n54\\\\t    filePath,\\\\n55\\\\t    registryPath: store.registryPath,\\\\n56\\\\t  });\\\\n57\\\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\\\n58\\\\t  const batches: MessageEventInput[][] = [\\\\n59\\\\t    [\\\\n60\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n61\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"reading it now\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n62\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", {\\\\n63\\\\t        payload: {\\\\n64\\\\t          toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-read-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n65\\\\t          toolName: \\\\\\\"read_file\\\\\\\",\\\\n66\\\\t          arguments: { path: \\\\\\\"notes.txt\\\\\\\" },\\\\n67\\\\t        },\\\\n68\\\\t      }),\\\\n69\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", {\\\\n70\\\\t        payload: { toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-read-1\\\\\\\", content: TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT, isError: false },\\\\n71\\\\t      }),\\\\n72\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n73\\\\t    ],\\\\n74\\\\t    [\\\\n75\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"summarize what you read\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n76\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"here is the summary\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n77\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n78\\\\t    ],\\\\n79\\\\t  ];\\\\n80\\\\t  for (const batch of batches) {\\\\n81\\\\t    const sent = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\\\n82\\\\t    if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\\\n83\\\\t  }\\\\n84\\\\t  const drained = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\\\n85\\\\t  if (!drained.ok) throw new Error(`fixture drain failed: ${drained.error.reason}`);\\\\n86\\\\t  if (drained.value.remaining !== 0) {\\\\n87\\\\t    throw new Error(`fixture drain left ${drained.value.remaining} items behind`);\\\\n88\\\\t  }\\\\n89\\\\t  return { filePath, sdk, double };\\\\n90\\\\t}\\\\n91\\\\t\\\\n92\\\\tfunction idsOf(result: { ok: boolean }): string[] {\\\\n93\\\\t  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(\\\\\\\"expected an ok list result\\\\\\\");\\\\n94\\\\t  return (result as { ok: true; value: Array<{ messageId: string }> }).value.map(\\\\n95\\\\t    (record) => record.messageId,\\\\n96\\\\t  );\\\\n97\\\\t}\\\\n98\\\\t\\\\n99\\\\t// The DD-6 observable-state snapshot: queued work through both owners, view\\\\n100\\\\t// boundary/zone through status, derived-form rows, and the event log. A read\\\\n101\\\\t// that mutates any of these fails the before/after deep-equal.\\\\n102\\\\tasync function observableState(filePath: string): Promise<Record<string, unknown>> {\\\\n103\\\\t  return {\\\\n104\\\\t    events: await intakeStream.listEvents({ filePath }),\\\\n105\\\\t    messageWork: await messages.listQueuedWork({ filePath }),\\\\n106\\\\t    turnWork: await turns.listQueuedWork({ filePath }),\\\\n107\\\\t    viewStatus: await threadView.status({ filePath }),\\\\n108\\\\t    forms: readDerivedForms(filePath),\\\\n109\\\\t  };\\\\n110\\\\t}\\\\n111\\\\t\\\\n112\\\\tlet store: TempStore;\\\\n113\\\\tbeforeEach(() => {\\\\n114\\\\t  store = tempStore();\\\\n115\\\\t});\\\\n116\\\\tafterEach(() => {\\\\n117\\\\t  store.cleanup();\\\\n118\\\\t});\\\\n119\\\\t\\\\n120\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.1 / AC-3.1: listing order, fields, and bounds\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n121\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"returns messages in record order with kind, token estimate, and turn membership\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n122\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n123\\\\t    const listed = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n124\\\\t    expect(listed.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n125\\\\t    if (!listed.ok) return;\\\\n126\\\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\\\n127\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\",\\\\n128\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\",\\\\n129\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\",\\\\n130\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\",\\\\n131\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\",\\\\n132\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\",\\\\n133\\\\t    ]);\\\\n134\\\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.sourceEventOrder)).toEqual([1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7]);\\\\n135\\\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.kind)).toEqual([\\\\n136\\\\t      \\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\",\\\\n137\\\\t      \\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\",\\\\n138\\\\t      \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\",\\\\n139\\\\t      \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\",\\\\n140\\\\t      \\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\",\\\\n141\\\\t      \\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\",\\\\n142\\\\t    ]);\\\\n143\\\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.turnId)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t2\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n144\\\\t    for (const record of listed.value) {\\\\n145\\\\t      expect(record.tokenEstimate).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\\\n146\\\\t      expect(record.deleted).toBeUndefined();\\\\n147\\\\t    }\\\\n148\\\\t  });\\\\n149\\\\t\\\\n150\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"honors from/to/limit windows exactly in source-event-order coordinates\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n151\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n152\\\\t    const windows: Array<[Parameters<typeof messages.listMessages>[1], string[]]> = [\\\\n153\\\\t      [{ from: 2, to: 4 }, [\\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n154\\\\t      [{ from: 6 }, [\\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n155\\\\t      [{ to: 2 }, [\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n156\\\\t      [{ limit: 3 }, [\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n157\\\\t      [{ from: 2, limit: 2 }, [\\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n158\\\\t      [{ from: 4, to: 4 }, [\\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n159\\\\t      [{ from: 5, to: 5 }, []], // the turn_end order: an event, never a message\\\\n160\\\\t    ];\\\\n161\\\\t    for (const [opts, expected] of windows) {\\\\n162\\\\t      expect(idsOf(await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts))).toEqual(expected);\\\\n163\\\\t    }\\\\n164\\\\t  });\\\\n165\\\\t\\\\n166\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"refuses bad bounds as caller errors and returns no partial window\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n167\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n168\\\\t    const badBounds = [{ from: 5, to: 2 }, { limit: 0 }, { limit: -1 }, { from: 1.5 }];\\\\n169\\\\t    for (const opts of badBounds) {\\\\n170\\\\t      const refused = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts);\\\\n171\\\\t      expect(refused.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n172\\\\t      if (refused.ok) continue;\\\\n173\\\\t      expect(refused.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\\\\\"caller_error\\\\\\\");\\\\n174\\\\t      expect(refused.error.code).toBe(\\\\\\\"invalid_bounds\\\\\\\");\\\\n175\\\\t    }\\\\n176\\\\t  });\\\\n177\\\\t});\\\\n178\\\\t\\\\n179\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.2 / AC-3.2: show returns the full record with owner-reported forms\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n180\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"a drained tool-result message comes back with full content, form states, and outcome metadata\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n181\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n182\\\\t    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n183\\\\t    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n184\\\\t    if (!shown.ok) return;\\\\n185\\\\t    const detail = shown.value;\\\\n186\\\\t    expect(detail.messageId).toBe(\\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n187\\\\t    expect(detail.kind).toBe(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\");\\\\n188\\\\t    expect(detail.turnId).toBe(\\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\");\\\\n189\\\\t    expect(detail.deleted).toBe(false);\\\\n190\\\\t    expect(detail.tokenEstimate).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\\\n191\\\\t    // The record, not the view: the complete original tool result verbatim.\\\\n192\\\\t    expect(detail.blocks).toHaveLength(1);\\\\n193\\\\t    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.blockType).toBe(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\");\\\\n194\\\\t    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\"]).toBe(TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT);\\\\n195\\\\t    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"toolCallId\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"call-read-1\\\\\\\");\\\\n196\\\\t    // Forms with states and tool-outcome metadata, joined from the owner.\\\\n197\\\\t    expect(detail.forms).toHaveLength(1);\\\\n198\\\\t    const summary = detail.forms[0];\\\\n199\\\\t    expect(summary?.form).toBe(\\\\\\\"tool_result_summary\\\\\\\");\\\\n200\\\\t    expect(summary?.state).toBe(\\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\");\\\\n201\\\\t    expect(summary?.content).toBeDefined();\\\\n202\\\\t    expect(summary?.metadata?.outcome).toBe(\\\\\\\"succeeded\\\\\\\");\\\\n203\\\\t    // Anti-shim: the forms ARE the owner report's entries for this message,\\\\n204\\\\t    // never a synthesized join (DD-2).\\\\n205\\\\t    const report = await messages.report({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\" });\\\\n206\\\\t    expect(report.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n207\\\\t    if (!report.ok) return;\\\\n208\\\\t    expect(detail.forms).toEqual(report.value);\\\\n209\\\\t  });\\\\n210\\\\t\\\\n211\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"a drained prompt shows its smoothing form alongside the full record\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n212\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n213\\\\t    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\");\\\\n214\\\\t    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n215\\\\t    if (!shown.ok) return;\\\\n216\\\\t    expect(shown.value.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\");\\\\n217\\\\t    expect(shown.value.forms.map((form) => [form.form, form.state])).toEqual([\\\\n218\\\\t      [\\\\\\\"smoothed_prompt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\"],\\\\n219\\\\t    ]);\\\\n220\\\\t  });\\\\n221\\\\t});\\\\n222\\\\t\\\\n223\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.3 / AC-3.3: deleted messages are audit-visible, never silently mixed\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n224\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"default list excludes a deleted message; include-deleted lists it marked; show returns it flagged\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n225\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n226\\\\t    const deleted = await messages.deleteMessage({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\" });\\\\n227\\\\t    expect(deleted.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n228\\\\t\\\\n229\\\\t    const defaultList = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n230\\\\t    expect(idsOf(defaultList)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n231\\\\t\\\\n232\\\\t    const audited = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { includeDeleted: true });\\\\n233\\\\t    expect(audited.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n234\\\\t    if (!audited.ok) return;\\\\n235\\\\t    expect(audited.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\\\n236\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\",\\\\n237\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\",\\\\n238\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\",\\\\n239\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\",\\\\n240\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\",\\\\n241\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\",\\\\n242\\\\t    ]);\\\\n243\\\\t    for (const record of audited.value) {\\\\n244\\\\t      if (record.messageId === \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\") expect(record.deleted).toBe(true);\\\\n245\\\\t      else expect(record.deleted).toBeUndefined();\\\\n246\\\\t    }\\\\n247\\\\t\\\\n248\\\\t    // Show on the deleted message is the audit read: the record, flagged —\\\\n249\\\\t    // never a not-found.\\\\n250\\\\t    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\");\\\\n251\\\\t    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n252\\\\t    if (!shown.ok) return;\\\\n253\\\\t    expect(shown.value.deleted).toBe(true);\\\\n254\\\\t    expect(shown.value.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"reading it now\\\\\\\");\\\\n255\\\\t  });\\\\n256\\\\t\\\\n257\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"show on a missing id is message_not_found\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n258\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n259\\\\t    const missing = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\");\\\\n260\\\\t    expect(missing.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n261\\\\t    if (missing.ok) return;\\\\n262\\\\t    expect(missing.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\\\\\"caller_error\\\\\\\");\\\\n263\\\\t    expect(missing.error.code).toBe(\\\\\\\"message_not_found\\\\\\\");\\\\n264\\\\t  });\\\\n265\\\\t});\\\\n266\\\\t\\\\n267\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"architecture risk: reads are read-only and provider-free (DD-6)\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n268\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"list and show in every mode leave observable state unchanged and call no provider\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n269\\\\t    const { filePath, double } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n270\\\\t    const captured = double.captureInputs();\\\\n271\\\\t    const before = await observableState(filePath);\\\\n272\\\\t\\\\n273\\\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n274\\\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 2, to: 4, limit: 2 });\\\\n275\\\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { includeDeleted: true });\\\\n276\\\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 9, to: 1 }); // refused, must not write either\\\\n277\\\\t    await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n278\\\\t    await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\"); // not-found, must not write either\\\\n279\\\\t\\\\n280\\\\t    const after = await observableState(filePath);\\\\n281\\\\t    expect(after).toEqual(before);\\\\n282\\\\t    expect(captured).toHaveLength(0);\\\\n283\\\\t  });\\\\n284\\\\t});\\\\n285\\\\t\\\\n286\\\\t// A thread with live, undrained work: one tool turn through a manual SDK\\\\n287\\\\t// (its no-op seam never drains), leaving three pending forms and their queue\\\\n288\\\\t// rows. The background read-only proof needs the pending state the manual\\\\n289\\\\t// read-only proof above cannot manufacture.\\\\n290\\\\tasync function pendingWorkThread(): Promise<string> {\\\\n291\\\\t  const seeder = createSdk({ provider: createProviderDouble(), mode: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\" });\\\\n292\\\\t  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\\\n293\\\\t  const created = await seeder.threads.newThread({\\\\n294\\\\t    filePath,\\\\n295\\\\t    registryPath: store.registryPath,\\\\n296\\\\t  });\\\\n297\\\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`pending fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\\\n298\\\\t  const sent = await seeder.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, [\\\\n299\\\\t    validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"background prompt\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n300\\\\t    validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", {\\\\n301\\\\t      payload: { toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-bg-1\\\\\\\", toolName: \\\\\\\"read_file\\\\\\\", arguments: { path: \\\\\\\"bg.txt\\\\\\\" } },\\\\n302\\\\t    }),\\\\n303\\\\t    validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", {\\\\n304\\\\t      payload: { toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-bg-1\\\\\\\", content: \\\\\\\"background output\\\\\\\", isError: false },\\\\n305\\\\t    }),\\\\n306\\\\t    validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"background answer\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n307\\\\t    validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n308\\\\t  ]);\\\\n309\\\\t  if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`pending fixture intake failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\\\n310\\\\t  return filePath;\\\\n311\\\\t}\\\\n312\\\\t\\\\n313\\\\t// Below-SDK raw snapshot of everything a wrongly-scheduled catch-up drain\\\\n314\\\\t// would move: work-item rows and derived-form states. Read through a raw\\\\n315\\\\t// handle (openRaw), never the SDK ops — those would fire their own touch and\\\\n316\\\\t// pollute the very state under test.\\\\n317\\\\tfunction rawWorkAndForms(filePath: string): Record<string, unknown> {\\\\n318\\\\t  const db = openRaw(filePath);\\\\n319\\\\t  try {\\\\n320\\\\t    return {\\\\n321\\\\t      workItems: db\\\\n322\\\\t        .prepare(`SELECT work_item_id, status, attempts FROM work_item ORDER BY work_item_id`)\\\\n323\\\\t        .all(),\\\\n324\\\\t      forms: db\\\\n325\\\\t        .prepare(\\\\n326\\\\t          `SELECT subject_id, form, state, source_version FROM derived_form\\\\n327\\\\t           ORDER BY subject_id, form`,\\\\n328\\\\t        )\\\\n329\\\\t        .all(),\\\\n330\\\\t    };\\\\n331\\\\t  } finally {\\\\n332\\\\t    db.close();\\\\n333\\\\t  }\\\\n334\\\\t}\\\\n335\\\\t\\\\n336\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"architecture risk: background reads schedule no catch-up drain (DD-6, SV-01-001)\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n337\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"list and show through a background SDK with pending work call no provider and advance no form\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n338\\\\t    const filePath = await pendingWorkThread();\\\\n339\\\\t\\\\n340\\\\t    // A fresh background SDK whose scheduler WOULD hang a first-touch catch-up\\\\n341\\\\t    // drain — and the provider call that drain makes — off the open\\\\n342\\\\t    // announcement (openThreadDatabase → fireThreadTouch → scheduler.touch) if\\\\n343\\\\t    // list or show fired it. The touch-suppressed read scope is what stops it;\\\\n344\\\\t    // this is the production-path proof a manual-mode no-op seam cannot give.\\\\n345\\\\t    const bgDouble = createProviderDouble();\\\\n346\\\\t    const bg = createSdk({ provider: bgDouble, mode: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\" });\\\\n347\\\\t    const captured = bgDouble.captureInputs();\\\\n348\\\\t    const before = rawWorkAndForms(filePath);\\\\n349\\\\t\\\\n350\\\\t    const listed = await bg.messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n351\\\\t    await bg.messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { limit: 1 });\\\\n352\\\\t    const shown = await bg.messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\");\\\\n353\\\\t    expect(listed.ok && shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n354\\\\t    if (!listed.ok || !shown.ok) return;\\\\n355\\\\t\\\\n356\\\\t    // The reads ran against the live, undrained queue — the records carry\\\\n357\\\\t    // their pending forms — so this is no vacuous pass on an empty thread.\\\\n358\\\\t    const listedForms = listed.value.flatMap((m) => m.forms ?? []);\\\\n359\\\\t    expect(listedForms.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\\\n360\\\\t    expect(listedForms.every((form) => form.state === \\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\")).toBe(true);\\\\n361\\\\t    expect(shown.value.forms.map((form) => form.state)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n362\\\\t\\\\n363\\\\t    // Give any wrongly-scheduled catch-up drain room to surface, then wait the\\\\n364\\\\t    // scheduler out before asserting nothing moved underneath the reads.\\\\n365\\\\t    await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 25));\\\\n366\\\\t    await bg.drainSettled({ filePath });\\\\n367\\\\t\\\\n368\\\\t    // Reads only: every work-item and form row is exactly as before, and the\\\\n369\\\\t    // background provider observed zero calls — no first-touch drain fired.\\\\n370\\\\t    expect(rawWorkAndForms(filePath)).toEqual(before);\\\\n371\\\\t    expect(captured).toHaveLength(0);\\\\n372\\\\t  });\\\\n373\\\\t});\\\\n374\\\\t\\\\n375\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"architecture risk: bounded listing loads only its window (AC-3.1, SV-01-002)\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n376\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"a bounded list excluding out-of-window rows never loads their blocks or forms\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n377\\\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n378\\\\t    // Corrupt content the bounds must exclude: m7's block (an out-of-window\\\\n379\\\\t    // message) and m4's tool-result-summary metadata (an out-of-window form).\\\\n380\\\\t    // Any read that loads either row throws on JSON.parse, so a bounded list\\\\n381\\\\t    // that still succeeds proves it never read outside its window.\\\\n382\\\\t    poisonMessageBlockJson(filePath, \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\");\\\\n383\\\\t    poisonMessageFormJson(filePath, \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n384\\\\t\\\\n385\\\\t    // In-window reads succeed and return exactly the window — the poisoned\\\\n386\\\\t    // rows are sourced neither as blocks nor as forms.\\\\n387\\\\t    for (const opts of [{ to: 1 }, { limit: 1 }] as const) {\\\\n388\\\\t      const bounded = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts);\\\\n389\\\\t      expect(bounded.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n390\\\\t      if (!bounded.ok) return;\\\\n391\\\\t      expect(bounded.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n392\\\\t      expect(bounded.value[0]?.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\");\\\\n393\\\\t    }\\\\n394\\\\t\\\\n395\\\\t    // Positive controls: a window that *includes* a poisoned row does load it\\\\n396\\\\t    // and fails on parse — proof the pills are real, so the passes above are\\\\n397\\\\t    // genuine no-loads, not silently-dropped output.\\\\n398\\\\t    const hitsBlock = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 7 });\\\\n399\\\\t    expect(hitsBlock.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n400\\\\t    const hitsForm = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 4, to: 4 });\\\\n401\\\\t    expect(hitsForm.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n402\\\\t  });\\\\n403\\\\t});\\\\n404\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"4b3be8a8-ca91-4c11-852b-e02aa44a56a6\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T13:24:18.421Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/messages-read.test.ts\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"// Story 1 (Epic 04), default suite: TC-3.1–3.3 — the message read surface.\\\\n// Bounded listing in source-event-order coordinates (DD-3), show returning\\\\n// the canonical record (full blocks, never view-shortened) composed with the\\\\n// owner report's form entries (DD-2), and the deleted-audit contract\\\\n// (excluded by default, listable flagged on request, show never not-found).\\\\n// Plus the architecture-risk legs: every read leaves observable state\\\\n// unchanged (read-only delta, DD-6) and calls no provider.\\\\nimport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\\\\\"vitest\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport {\\\\n  createSdk,\\\\n  intakeStream,\\\\n  messages,\\\\n  threadView,\\\\n  turns,\\\\n  type Lhc,\\\\n  type MessageEventInput,\\\\n} from \\\\\\\"../src/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport {\\\\n  createProviderDouble,\\\\n  openRaw,\\\\n  poisonMessageBlockJson,\\\\n  poisonMessageFormJson,\\\\n  readDerivedForms,\\\\n  tempStore,\\\\n  validEvent,\\\\n  type TempStore,\\\\n} from \\\\\\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n// Long enough that any view-form shortening would be visible: show must\\\\n// return this verbatim (AC-3.2's record-not-view contract).\\\\nconst TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT = [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"contents of notes.txt — full record content:\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"line 1: the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"line 2: detailed tool output that a boundary-shortened form would drop\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"line 3: trailing detail proving the record came back complete\\\\\\\",\\\\n].join(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\");\\\\n\\\\ninterface ReadFixture {\\\\n  filePath: string;\\\\n  sdk: Lhc;\\\\n  double: ReturnType<typeof createProviderDouble>;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// Two closed turns through real intake, fully drained against the\\\\n// deterministic double so m1's smoothing and m3/m4's tool summaries sit\\\\n// ready with mechanically stamped outcome metadata. Messages: m1 prompt,\\\\n// m2 text, m3 call, m4 result (turn 1; turn_end is event 5, no message);\\\\n// m6 prompt, m7 text (turn 2). Source event orders 1,2,3,4,6,7.\\\\nasync function readFixture(store: TempStore): Promise<ReadFixture> {\\\\n  const double = createProviderDouble();\\\\n  const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\" });\\\\n  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\\\n  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({\\\\n    filePath,\\\\n    registryPath: store.registryPath,\\\\n  });\\\\n  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\\\n  const batches: MessageEventInput[][] = [\\\\n    [\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"reading it now\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", {\\\\n        payload: {\\\\n          toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-read-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n          toolName: \\\\\\\"read_file\\\\\\\",\\\\n          arguments: { path: \\\\\\\"notes.txt\\\\\\\" },\\\\n        },\\\\n      }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", {\\\\n        payload: { toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-read-1\\\\\\\", content: TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT, isError: false },\\\\n      }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n    ],\\\\n    [\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"summarize what you read\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"here is the summary\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n    ],\\\\n  ];\\\\n  for (const batch of batches) {\\\\n    const sent = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\\\n    if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\\\n  }\\\\n  const drained = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\\\n  if (!drained.ok) throw new Error(`fixture drain failed: ${drained.error.reason}`);\\\\n  if (drained.value.remaining !== 0) {\\\\n    throw new Error(`fixture drain left ${drained.value.remaining} items behind`);\\\\n  }\\\\n  return { filePath, sdk, double };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nfunction idsOf(result: { ok: boolean }): string[] {\\\\n  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(\\\\\\\"expected an ok list result\\\\\\\");\\\\n  return (result as { ok: true; value: Array<{ messageId: string }> }).value.map(\\\\n    (record) => record.messageId,\\\\n  );\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// The DD-6 observable-state snapshot: queued work through both owners, view\\\\n// boundary/zone through status, derived-form rows, and the event log. A read\\\\n// that mutates any of these fails the before/after deep-equal.\\\\nasync function observableState(filePath: string): Promise<Record<string, unknown>> {\\\\n  return {\\\\n    events: await intakeStream.listEvents({ filePath }),\\\\n    messageWork: await messages.listQueuedWork({ filePath }),\\\\n    turnWork: await turns.listQueuedWork({ filePath }),\\\\n    viewStatus: await threadView.status({ filePath }),\\\\n    forms: readDerivedForms(filePath),\\\\n  };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nlet store: TempStore;\\\\nbeforeEach(() => {\\\\n  store = tempStore();\\\\n});\\\\nafterEach(() => {\\\\n  store.cleanup();\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.1 / AC-3.1: listing order, fields, and bounds\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"returns messages in record order with kind, token estimate, and turn membership\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const listed = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n    expect(listed.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (!listed.ok) return;\\\\n    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\",\\\\n    ]);\\\\n    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.sourceEventOrder)).toEqual([1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7]);\\\\n    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.kind)).toEqual([\\\\n      \\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\",\\\\n    ]);\\\\n    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.turnId)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"t2\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n    for (const record of listed.value) {\\\\n      expect(record.tokenEstimate).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\\\n      expect(record.deleted).toBeUndefined();\\\\n    }\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"honors from/to/limit windows exactly in source-event-order coordinates\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const windows: Array<[Parameters<typeof messages.listMessages>[1], string[]]> = [\\\\n      [{ from: 2, to: 4 }, [\\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n      [{ from: 6 }, [\\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n      [{ to: 2 }, [\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n      [{ limit: 3 }, [\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n      [{ from: 2, limit: 2 }, [\\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n      [{ from: 4, to: 4 }, [\\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\"]],\\\\n      [{ from: 5, to: 5 }, []], // the turn_end order: an event, never a message\\\\n    ];\\\\n    for (const [opts, expected] of windows) {\\\\n      expect(idsOf(await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts))).toEqual(expected);\\\\n    }\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"refuses bad bounds as caller errors and returns no partial window\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const badBounds = [{ from: 5, to: 2 }, { limit: 0 }, { limit: -1 }, { from: 1.5 }];\\\\n    for (const opts of badBounds) {\\\\n      const refused = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts);\\\\n      expect(refused.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n      if (refused.ok) continue;\\\\n      expect(refused.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\\\\\"caller_error\\\\\\\");\\\\n      expect(refused.error.code).toBe(\\\\\\\"invalid_bounds\\\\\\\");\\\\n    }\\\\n  });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.2 / AC-3.2: show returns the full record with owner-reported forms\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"a drained tool-result message comes back with full content, form states, and outcome metadata\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (!shown.ok) return;\\\\n    const detail = shown.value;\\\\n    expect(detail.messageId).toBe(\\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(detail.kind).toBe(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(detail.turnId).toBe(\\\\\\\"t1\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(detail.deleted).toBe(false);\\\\n    expect(detail.tokenEstimate).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\\\n    // The record, not the view: the complete original tool result verbatim.\\\\n    expect(detail.blocks).toHaveLength(1);\\\\n    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.blockType).toBe(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\"]).toBe(TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT);\\\\n    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"toolCallId\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"call-read-1\\\\\\\");\\\\n    // Forms with states and tool-outcome metadata, joined from the owner.\\\\n    expect(detail.forms).toHaveLength(1);\\\\n    const summary = detail.forms[0];\\\\n    expect(summary?.form).toBe(\\\\\\\"tool_result_summary\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(summary?.state).toBe(\\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(summary?.content).toBeDefined();\\\\n    expect(summary?.metadata?.outcome).toBe(\\\\\\\"succeeded\\\\\\\");\\\\n    // Anti-shim: the forms ARE the owner report's entries for this message,\\\\n    // never a synthesized join (DD-2).\\\\n    const report = await messages.report({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\" });\\\\n    expect(report.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (!report.ok) return;\\\\n    expect(detail.forms).toEqual(report.value);\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"a drained prompt shows its smoothing form alongside the full record\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (!shown.ok) return;\\\\n    expect(shown.value.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(shown.value.forms.map((form) => [form.form, form.state])).toEqual([\\\\n      [\\\\\\\"smoothed_prompt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\"],\\\\n    ]);\\\\n  });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.3 / AC-3.3: deleted messages are audit-visible, never silently mixed\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"default list excludes a deleted message; include-deleted lists it marked; show returns it flagged\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const deleted = await messages.deleteMessage({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\" });\\\\n    expect(deleted.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n\\\\n    const defaultList = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n    expect(idsOf(defaultList)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n\\\\n    const audited = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { includeDeleted: true });\\\\n    expect(audited.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (!audited.ok) return;\\\\n    expect(audited.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m3\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m6\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\",\\\\n    ]);\\\\n    for (const record of audited.value) {\\\\n      if (record.messageId === \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\") expect(record.deleted).toBe(true);\\\\n      else expect(record.deleted).toBeUndefined();\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    // Show on the deleted message is the audit read: the record, flagged —\\\\n    // never a not-found.\\\\n    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (!shown.ok) return;\\\\n    expect(shown.value.deleted).toBe(true);\\\\n    expect(shown.value.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"reading it now\\\\\\\");\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"show on a missing id is message_not_found\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const missing = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(missing.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n    if (missing.ok) return;\\\\n    expect(missing.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\\\\\"caller_error\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(missing.error.code).toBe(\\\\\\\"message_not_found\\\\\\\");\\\\n  });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"architecture risk: reads are read-only and provider-free (DD-6)\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"list and show in every mode leave observable state unchanged and call no provider\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath, double } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    const captured = double.captureInputs();\\\\n    const before = await observableState(filePath);\\\\n\\\\n    await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 2, to: 4, limit: 2 });\\\\n    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { includeDeleted: true });\\\\n    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 9, to: 1 }); // refused, must not write either\\\\n    await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n    await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\"); // not-found, must not write either\\\\n\\\\n    const after = await observableState(filePath);\\\\n    expect(after).toEqual(before);\\\\n    expect(captured).toHaveLength(0);\\\\n  });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\n// A thread with live, undrained work: one tool turn through a manual SDK\\\\n// (its no-op seam never drains), leaving three pending forms and their queue\\\\n// rows. The background read-only proof needs the pending state the manual\\\\n// read-only proof above cannot manufacture.\\\\nasync function pendingWorkThread(): Promise<string> {\\\\n  const seeder = createSdk({ provider: createProviderDouble(), mode: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\" });\\\\n  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\\\n  const created = await seeder.threads.newThread({\\\\n    filePath,\\\\n    registryPath: store.registryPath,\\\\n  });\\\\n  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`pending fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\\\n  const sent = await seeder.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, [\\\\n    validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"background prompt\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n    validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", {\\\\n      payload: { toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-bg-1\\\\\\\", toolName: \\\\\\\"read_file\\\\\\\", arguments: { path: \\\\\\\"bg.txt\\\\\\\" } },\\\\n    }),\\\\n    validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", {\\\\n      payload: { toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-bg-1\\\\\\\", content: \\\\\\\"background output\\\\\\\", isError: false },\\\\n    }),\\\\n    validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"background answer\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n    validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n  ]);\\\\n  if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`pending fixture intake failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\\\n  return filePath;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// Below-SDK raw snapshot of everything a wrongly-scheduled catch-up drain\\\\n// would move: work-item rows and derived-form states. Read through a raw\\\\n// handle (openRaw), never the SDK ops — those would fire their own touch and\\\\n// pollute the very state under test.\\\\nfunction rawWorkAndForms(filePath: string): Record<string, unknown> {\\\\n  const db = openRaw(filePath);\\\\n  try {\\\\n    return {\\\\n      workItems: db\\\\n        .prepare(`SELECT work_item_id, status, attempts FROM work_item ORDER BY work_item_id`)\\\\n        .all(),\\\\n      forms: db\\\\n        .prepare(\\\\n          `SELECT subject_id, form, state, source_version FROM derived_form\\\\n           ORDER BY subject_id, form`,\\\\n        )\\\\n        .all(),\\\\n    };\\\\n  } finally {\\\\n    db.close();\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"architecture risk: background reads schedule no catch-up drain (DD-6, SV-01-001)\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"list and show through a background SDK with pending work call no provider and advance no form\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const filePath = await pendingWorkThread();\\\\n\\\\n    // A fresh background SDK whose scheduler WOULD hang a first-touch catch-up\\\\n    // drain — and the provider call that drain makes — off the open\\\\n    // announcement (openThreadDatabase → fireThreadTouch → scheduler.touch) if\\\\n    // list or show fired it. The touch-suppressed read scope is what stops it;\\\\n    // this is the production-path proof a manual-mode no-op seam cannot give.\\\\n    const bgDouble = createProviderDouble();\\\\n    const bg = createSdk({ provider: bgDouble, mode: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\" });\\\\n    const captured = bgDouble.captureInputs();\\\\n    const before = rawWorkAndForms(filePath);\\\\n\\\\n    const listed = await bg.messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\\\n    await bg.messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { limit: 1 });\\\\n    const shown = await bg.messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(listed.ok && shown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (!listed.ok || !shown.ok) return;\\\\n\\\\n    // The reads ran against the live, undrained queue — the records carry\\\\n    // their pending forms — so this is no vacuous pass on an empty thread.\\\\n    const listedForms = listed.value.flatMap((m) => m.forms ?? []);\\\\n    expect(listedForms.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\\\n    expect(listedForms.every((form) => form.state === \\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\")).toBe(true);\\\\n    expect(shown.value.forms.map((form) => form.state)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n\\\\n    // Give any wrongly-scheduled catch-up drain room to surface, then wait the\\\\n    // scheduler out before asserting nothing moved underneath the reads.\\\\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 25));\\\\n    await bg.drainSettled({ filePath });\\\\n\\\\n    // Reads only: every work-item and form row is exactly as before, and the\\\\n    // background provider observed zero calls — no first-touch drain fired.\\\\n    expect(rawWorkAndForms(filePath)).toEqual(before);\\\\n    expect(captured).toHaveLength(0);\\\\n  });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"architecture risk: bounded listing loads only its window (AC-3.1, SV-01-002)\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"a bounded list excluding out-of-window rows never loads their blocks or forms\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\\\n    // Corrupt content the bounds must exclude: m7's block (an out-of-window\\\\n    // message) and m4's tool-result-summary metadata (an out-of-window form).\\\\n    // Any read that loads either row throws on JSON.parse, so a bounded list\\\\n    // that still succeeds proves it never read outside its window.\\\\n    poisonMessageBlockJson(filePath, \\\\\\\"m7\\\\\\\");\\\\n    poisonMessageFormJson(filePath, \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\");\\\\n\\\\n    // In-window reads succeed and return exactly the window — the poisoned\\\\n    // rows are sourced neither as blocks nor as forms.\\\\n    for (const opts of [{ to: 1 }, { limit: 1 }] as const) {\\\\n      const bounded = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts);\\\\n      expect(bounded.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n      if (!bounded.ok) return;\\\\n      expect(bounded.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\\\\\\"m1\\\\\\\"]);\\\\n      expect(bounded.value[0]?.blocks[0]?.content[\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\"]).toBe(\\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\");\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    // Positive controls: a window that *includes* a poisoned row does load it\\\\n    // and fails on parse — proof the pills are real, so the passes above are\\\\n    // genuine no-loads, not silently-dropped output.\\\\n    const hitsBlock = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 7 });\\\\n    expect(hitsBlock.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n    const hitsForm = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 4, to: 4 });\\\\n    expect(hitsForm.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n  });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":404,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":404}}}\\n132:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01Ke6Z8o4LHDnywvr9Stkrui\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t// Story 1 (Epic 04), process-boundary suite: TC-3.4 — `lhc messages list`\\\\n2\\\\t// and `lhc messages show` through the spawned dist/cli.js have full JSON\\\\n3\\\\t// parity with the in-process SDK operations: same options, same result JSON,\\\\n4\\\\t// refusals included. Reads are non-mutating, so one fixture thread serves\\\\n5\\\\t// both sides — the spawned output deep-equals the SDK result on the same\\\\n6\\\\t// file (the production-path proof: cli/messages-read.ts routes to the SDK,\\\\n7\\\\t// any divergence is a bypass). Reads need no provider; the binary runs with\\\\n8\\\\t// LHC_PROVIDER unset. Runs under verify-all only (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1).\\\\n9\\\\t// TC-5.4's checkpoint parity joins this file in Story 4.\\\\n10\\\\timport { spawnSync } from \\\\\\\"node:child_process\\\\\\\";\\\\n11\\\\timport { mkdtempSync, rmSync } from \\\\\\\"node:fs\\\\\\\";\\\\n12\\\\timport { tmpdir } from \\\\\\\"node:os\\\\\\\";\\\\n13\\\\timport path from \\\\\\\"node:path\\\\\\\";\\\\n14\\\\timport { fileURLToPath } from \\\\\\\"node:url\\\\\\\";\\\\n15\\\\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\\\\\"vitest\\\\\\\";\\\\n16\\\\timport {\\\\n17\\\\t  createSdk,\\\\n18\\\\t  messages,\\\\n19\\\\t  resolveNamedProvider,\\\\n20\\\\t  threads,\\\\n21\\\\t  type MessageListOptions,\\\\n22\\\\t} from \\\\\\\"../src/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n23\\\\timport { validEvent } from \\\\\\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n24\\\\t\\\\n25\\\\tconst pkgRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \\\\\\\"..\\\\\\\");\\\\n26\\\\tconst cliPath = path.join(pkgRoot, \\\\\\\"dist\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"cli.js\\\\\\\");\\\\n27\\\\t\\\\n28\\\\tfunction runBinary(args: string[]): { status: number | null; stdout: string; stderr: string } {\\\\n29\\\\t  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [cliPath, ...args], {\\\\n30\\\\t    encoding: \\\\\\\"utf8\\\\\\\",\\\\n31\\\\t    env: { ...process.env, LHC_PROVIDER: undefined },\\\\n32\\\\t  });\\\\n33\\\\t  return { status: result.status, stdout: result.stdout, stderr: result.stderr };\\\\n34\\\\t}\\\\n35\\\\t\\\\n36\\\\tlet dir: string;\\\\n37\\\\tbeforeEach(() => {\\\\n38\\\\t  dir = mkdtempSync(path.join(tmpdir(), \\\\\\\"lhc-proc-inspect-\\\\\\\"));\\\\n39\\\\t});\\\\n40\\\\tafterEach(() => {\\\\n41\\\\t  rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\\\\n42\\\\t});\\\\n43\\\\t\\\\n44\\\\t// Two closed turns (m1 prompt, m2 text, m3 call, m4 result; m6 prompt,\\\\n45\\\\t// m7 text), drained in-process against the registry's deterministic\\\\n46\\\\t// provider, then m2 deleted — so the parity sweep covers live, bounded,\\\\n47\\\\t// deleted-included, and deleted-shown reads on one record.\\\\n48\\\\tasync function seedThread(): Promise<string> {\\\\n49\\\\t  const filePath = path.join(dir, \\\\\\\"inspect-parity.sqlite\\\\\\\");\\\\n50\\\\t  const created = await threads.newThread({\\\\n51\\\\t    filePath,\\\\n52\\\\t    registryPath: path.join(dir, \\\\\\\"registry.sqlite\\\\\\\"),\\\\n53\\\\t  });\\\\n54\\\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\\\n55\\\\t  const provider = resolveNamedProvider(\\\\\\\"deterministic\\\\\\\");\\\\n56\\\\t  if (provider === undefined) throw new Error(\\\\\\\"deterministic provider not registered\\\\\\\");\\\\n57\\\\t  const sdk = createSdk({ provider, mode: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\" });\\\\n58\\\\t  const batches = [\\\\n59\\\\t    [\\\\n60\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n61\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"reading it now\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n62\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", {\\\\n63\\\\t        payload: {\\\\n64\\\\t          toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-parity-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n65\\\\t          toolName: \\\\\\\"read_file\\\\\\\",\\\\n66\\\\t          arguments: { path: \\\\\\\"notes.txt\\\\\\\" },\\\\n67\\\\t        },\\\\n68\\\\t      }),\\\\n69\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", {\\\\n70\\\\t        payload: {\\\\n71\\\\t          toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-parity-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n72\\\\t          content: \\\\\\\"contents of notes.txt: full parity-fixture tool output\\\\\\\",\\\\n73\\\\t          isError: false,\\\\n74\\\\t        },\\\\n75\\\\t      }),\\\\n76\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n77\\\\t    ],\\\\n78\\\\t    [\\\\n79\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"summarize what you read\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n80\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"here is the summary\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n81\\\\t      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n82\\\\t    ],\\\\n83\\\\t  ];\\\\n84\\\\t  for (const batch of batches) {\\\\n85\\\\t    const sent = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\\\n86\\\\t    if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\\\n87\\\\t  }\\\\n88\\\\t  const drained = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\\\n89\\\\t  if (!drained.ok || drained.value.remaining !== 0) {\\\\n90\\\\t    throw new Error(\\\\\\\"fixture drain did not settle\\\\\\\");\\\\n91\\\\t  }\\\\n92\\\\t  const deleted = await messages.deleteMessage({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\" });\\\\n93\\\\t  if (!deleted.ok) throw new Error(`fixture delete failed: ${deleted.error.reason}`);\\\\n94\\\\t  return filePath;\\\\n95\\\\t}\\\\n96\\\\t\\\\n97\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.4 / AC-3.4: spawned-CLI message list/show parity with the SDK\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n98\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"messages list mirrors the SDK across default, bounded, include-deleted, and refused options\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n99\\\\t    const filePath = await seedThread();\\\\n100\\\\t    const cases: Array<{ args: string[]; opts: MessageListOptions; ok: boolean }> = [\\\\n101\\\\t      { args: [], opts: {}, ok: true },\\\\n102\\\\t      { args: [\\\\\\\"--from\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--to\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\"], opts: { from: 2, to: 4 }, ok: true },\\\\n103\\\\t      { args: [\\\\\\\"--limit\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\"], opts: { limit: 2 }, ok: true },\\\\n104\\\\t      { args: [\\\\\\\"--include-deleted\\\\\\\"], opts: { includeDeleted: true }, ok: true },\\\\n105\\\\t      {\\\\n106\\\\t        args: [\\\\\\\"--from\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--limit\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--include-deleted\\\\\\\"],\\\\n107\\\\t        opts: { from: 3, limit: 2, includeDeleted: true },\\\\n108\\\\t        ok: true,\\\\n109\\\\t      },\\\\n110\\\\t      // The refusal leg: bad bounds carry the same structured error through\\\\n111\\\\t      // the process boundary, exit 1.\\\\n112\\\\t      { args: [\\\\\\\"--from\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--to\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\"], opts: { from: 5, to: 2 }, ok: false },\\\\n113\\\\t    ];\\\\n114\\\\t    for (const parity of cases) {\\\\n115\\\\t      const viaSdk = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, parity.opts);\\\\n116\\\\t      expect(viaSdk.ok).toBe(parity.ok);\\\\n117\\\\t      const viaCli = runBinary([\\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"list\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--file-path\\\\\\\", filePath, ...parity.args]);\\\\n118\\\\t      expect(viaCli.status).toBe(parity.ok ? 0 : 1);\\\\n119\\\\t      expect(JSON.parse(viaCli.stdout)).toEqual(viaSdk);\\\\n120\\\\t    }\\\\n121\\\\t    // Six serial dist/cli.js spawns push past Vitest's 5000ms default on a\\\\n122\\\\t    // loaded machine; the explicit budget keeps the configured verify-all gate\\\\n123\\\\t    // stable (SV-01-003), matching the other process-suite spawn tests.\\\\n124\\\\t  }, 30000);\\\\n125\\\\t\\\\n126\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"messages show mirrors the SDK for live, deleted, and missing targets\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n127\\\\t    const filePath = await seedThread();\\\\n128\\\\t    for (const messageId of [\\\\n129\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\", // live drained tool result, forms attached\\\\n130\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", // deleted: ok + flag — the audit read\\\\n131\\\\t      \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\", // missing: message_not_found, exit 1\\\\n132\\\\t    ]) {\\\\n133\\\\t      const viaSdk = await messages.show({ filePath }, messageId);\\\\n134\\\\t      const viaCli = runBinary([\\\\n135\\\\t        \\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\",\\\\n136\\\\t        \\\\\\\"show\\\\\\\",\\\\n137\\\\t        \\\\\\\"--file-path\\\\\\\",\\\\n138\\\\t        filePath,\\\\n139\\\\t        \\\\\\\"--message-id\\\\\\\",\\\\n140\\\\t        messageId,\\\\n141\\\\t      ]);\\\\n142\\\\t      expect(viaCli.status).toBe(viaSdk.ok ? 0 : 1);\\\\n143\\\\t      expect(JSON.parse(viaCli.stdout)).toEqual(viaSdk);\\\\n144\\\\t    }\\\\n145\\\\t    // The deleted target succeeds with the flag; the missing one refuses —\\\\n146\\\\t    // pinned here so the loop's parity can't both-sides-drift.\\\\n147\\\\t    const deletedShown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\");\\\\n148\\\\t    expect(deletedShown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n149\\\\t    if (deletedShown.ok) expect(deletedShown.value.deleted).toBe(true);\\\\n150\\\\t    const missing = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\");\\\\n151\\\\t    expect(missing.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n152\\\\t    if (!missing.ok) expect(missing.error.code).toBe(\\\\\\\"message_not_found\\\\\\\");\\\\n153\\\\t    // Same spawn-cost budget as the list leg, for the same gate-stability\\\\n154\\\\t    // reason (SV-01-003).\\\\n155\\\\t  }, 30000);\\\\n156\\\\t});\\\\n157\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"0514ced0-61a4-4490-b296-69e25eabcc5e\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T13:24:19.012Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"// Story 1 (Epic 04), process-boundary suite: TC-3.4 — `lhc messages list`\\\\n// and `lhc messages show` through the spawned dist/cli.js have full JSON\\\\n// parity with the in-process SDK operations: same options, same result JSON,\\\\n// refusals included. Reads are non-mutating, so one fixture thread serves\\\\n// both sides — the spawned output deep-equals the SDK result on the same\\\\n// file (the production-path proof: cli/messages-read.ts routes to the SDK,\\\\n// any divergence is a bypass). Reads need no provider; the binary runs with\\\\n// LHC_PROVIDER unset. Runs under verify-all only (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1).\\\\n// TC-5.4's checkpoint parity joins this file in Story 4.\\\\nimport { spawnSync } from \\\\\\\"node:child_process\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { mkdtempSync, rmSync } from \\\\\\\"node:fs\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { tmpdir } from \\\\\\\"node:os\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport path from \\\\\\\"node:path\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \\\\\\\"node:url\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\\\\\"vitest\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport {\\\\n  createSdk,\\\\n  messages,\\\\n  resolveNamedProvider,\\\\n  threads,\\\\n  type MessageListOptions,\\\\n} from \\\\\\\"../src/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { validEvent } from \\\\\\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\nconst pkgRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \\\\\\\"..\\\\\\\");\\\\nconst cliPath = path.join(pkgRoot, \\\\\\\"dist\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"cli.js\\\\\\\");\\\\n\\\\nfunction runBinary(args: string[]): { status: number | null; stdout: string; stderr: string } {\\\\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [cliPath, ...args], {\\\\n    encoding: \\\\\\\"utf8\\\\\\\",\\\\n    env: { ...process.env, LHC_PROVIDER: undefined },\\\\n  });\\\\n  return { status: result.status, stdout: result.stdout, stderr: result.stderr };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nlet dir: string;\\\\nbeforeEach(() => {\\\\n  dir = mkdtempSync(path.join(tmpdir(), \\\\\\\"lhc-proc-inspect-\\\\\\\"));\\\\n});\\\\nafterEach(() => {\\\\n  rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\n// Two closed turns (m1 prompt, m2 text, m3 call, m4 result; m6 prompt,\\\\n// m7 text), drained in-process against the registry's deterministic\\\\n// provider, then m2 deleted — so the parity sweep covers live, bounded,\\\\n// deleted-included, and deleted-shown reads on one record.\\\\nasync function seedThread(): Promise<string> {\\\\n  const filePath = path.join(dir, \\\\\\\"inspect-parity.sqlite\\\\\\\");\\\\n  const created = await threads.newThread({\\\\n    filePath,\\\\n    registryPath: path.join(dir, \\\\\\\"registry.sqlite\\\\\\\"),\\\\n  });\\\\n  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\\\n  const provider = resolveNamedProvider(\\\\\\\"deterministic\\\\\\\");\\\\n  if (provider === undefined) throw new Error(\\\\\\\"deterministic provider not registered\\\\\\\");\\\\n  const sdk = createSdk({ provider, mode: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\" });\\\\n  const batches = [\\\\n    [\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"please read notes.txt\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"reading it now\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", {\\\\n        payload: {\\\\n          toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-parity-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n          toolName: \\\\\\\"read_file\\\\\\\",\\\\n          arguments: { path: \\\\\\\"notes.txt\\\\\\\" },\\\\n        },\\\\n      }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", {\\\\n        payload: {\\\\n          toolCallId: \\\\\\\"call-parity-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n          content: \\\\\\\"contents of notes.txt: full parity-fixture tool output\\\\\\\",\\\\n          isError: false,\\\\n        },\\\\n      }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n    ],\\\\n    [\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"summarize what you read\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\", { payload: { text: \\\\\\\"here is the summary\\\\\\\" } }),\\\\n      validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\"),\\\\n    ],\\\\n  ];\\\\n  for (const batch of batches) {\\\\n    const sent = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\\\n    if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\\\n  }\\\\n  const drained = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\\\n  if (!drained.ok || drained.value.remaining !== 0) {\\\\n    throw new Error(\\\\\\\"fixture drain did not settle\\\\\\\");\\\\n  }\\\\n  const deleted = await messages.deleteMessage({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\" });\\\\n  if (!deleted.ok) throw new Error(`fixture delete failed: ${deleted.error.reason}`);\\\\n  return filePath;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"TC-3.4 / AC-3.4: spawned-CLI message list/show parity with the SDK\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"messages list mirrors the SDK across default, bounded, include-deleted, and refused options\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const filePath = await seedThread();\\\\n    const cases: Array<{ args: string[]; opts: MessageListOptions; ok: boolean }> = [\\\\n      { args: [], opts: {}, ok: true },\\\\n      { args: [\\\\\\\"--from\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--to\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\"], opts: { from: 2, to: 4 }, ok: true },\\\\n      { args: [\\\\\\\"--limit\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\"], opts: { limit: 2 }, ok: true },\\\\n      { args: [\\\\\\\"--include-deleted\\\\\\\"], opts: { includeDeleted: true }, ok: true },\\\\n      {\\\\n        args: [\\\\\\\"--from\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--limit\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--include-deleted\\\\\\\"],\\\\n        opts: { from: 3, limit: 2, includeDeleted: true },\\\\n        ok: true,\\\\n      },\\\\n      // The refusal leg: bad bounds carry the same structured error through\\\\n      // the process boundary, exit 1.\\\\n      { args: [\\\\\\\"--from\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--to\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\"], opts: { from: 5, to: 2 }, ok: false },\\\\n    ];\\\\n    for (const parity of cases) {\\\\n      const viaSdk = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, parity.opts);\\\\n      expect(viaSdk.ok).toBe(parity.ok);\\\\n      const viaCli = runBinary([\\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"list\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--file-path\\\\\\\", filePath, ...parity.args]);\\\\n      expect(viaCli.status).toBe(parity.ok ? 0 : 1);\\\\n      expect(JSON.parse(viaCli.stdout)).toEqual(viaSdk);\\\\n    }\\\\n    // Six serial dist/cli.js spawns push past Vitest's 5000ms default on a\\\\n    // loaded machine; the explicit budget keeps the configured verify-all gate\\\\n    // stable (SV-01-003), matching the other process-suite spawn tests.\\\\n  }, 30000);\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"messages show mirrors the SDK for live, deleted, and missing targets\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const filePath = await seedThread();\\\\n    for (const messageId of [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m4\\\\\\\", // live drained tool result, forms attached\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\", // deleted: ok + flag — the audit read\\\\n      \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\", // missing: message_not_found, exit 1\\\\n    ]) {\\\\n      const viaSdk = await messages.show({ filePath }, messageId);\\\\n      const viaCli = runBinary([\\\\n        \\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"show\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"--file-path\\\\\\\",\\\\n        filePath,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"--message-id\\\\\\\",\\\\n        messageId,\\\\n      ]);\\\\n      expect(viaCli.status).toBe(viaSdk.ok ? 0 : 1);\\\\n      expect(JSON.parse(viaCli.stdout)).toEqual(viaSdk);\\\\n    }\\\\n    // The deleted target succeeds with the flag; the missing one refuses —\\\\n    // pinned here so the loop's parity can't both-sides-drift.\\\\n    const deletedShown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m2\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(deletedShown.ok).toBe(true);\\\\n    if (deletedShown.ok) expect(deletedShown.value.deleted).toBe(true);\\\\n    const missing = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\\\\\"m99\\\\\\\");\\\\n    expect(missing.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n    if (!missing.ok) expect(missing.error.code).toBe(\\\\\\\"message_not_found\\\\\\\");\\\\n    // Same spawn-cost budget as the list leg, for the same gate-stability\\\\n    // reason (SV-01-003).\\\\n  }, 30000);\\\\n});\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":157,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":157}}}\\n158:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"content_block_delta\\\",\\\"index\\\":1,\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_delta\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\" at the supporting infrastructure — the touch-suppression context, forms read, fixtures, and run the tests to see the act\\\"}},\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"a5ccbf52-a6ef-4869-a994-848db13ed2c3\\\"}\\n160:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-4-8\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_01HcNe1CeM8QTMAg2hFYwTxs\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Now let me look at the supporting infrastructure — the touch-suppression context, forms read, fixtures, and run the tests to see the actual current state.\\\"}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":131,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":14545,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":51039,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":14545},\\\"output_tokens\\\":3,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"not_available\\\"},\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"0be3567c-f897-4afa-ae99-5feabd953dc4\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CbySRsoDegfKR183TXaiw\\\"}\\n174:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01HxrP7bVV93ZzEfjYQ2d2L4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t// Message-domain reads for derivation (Flow 2): the handler's view of its\\\\n2\\\\t// source message and the call-id pairing reads — the only reach a\\\\n3\\\\t// message-level handler has beyond its own message (AC-2.5). Also the\\\\n4\\\\t// late-result repair lookup intake's projection step runs (AC-2.8): one\\\\n5\\\\t// indexed query by call id, never a scan (the v5 expression index on\\\\n6\\\\t// message_block covers it) and never a drain-time sweep or read-time join.\\\\n7\\\\t// Completion writes for message forms ride the work-queue util's `complete`\\\\n8\\\\t// (Story 1): UPDATE-only with the source-version check — no write path here.\\\\n9\\\\t// Read-back of message-owned form rows (the listMessages join) also lives\\\\n10\\\\t// here: stored state returned as stored — never re-derived on read.\\\\n11\\\\timport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\\\\\"node:sqlite\\\\\\\";\\\\n12\\\\timport type {\\\\n13\\\\t  DependencyGap,\\\\n14\\\\t  DerivedForm,\\\\n15\\\\t  DerivedFormMetadata,\\\\n16\\\\t  DerivedFormState,\\\\n17\\\\t  FormKind,\\\\n18\\\\t  FormReportEntry,\\\\n19\\\\t} from \\\\\\\"../../../shared/derivation.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n20\\\\timport { reportEntryFromRow, type RawReportRow } from \\\\\\\"../../../shared/report.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n21\\\\t\\\\n22\\\\texport interface MessageSource {\\\\n23\\\\t  messageId: string;\\\\n24\\\\t  kind: string;\\\\n25\\\\t  blocks: Array<{ blockType: string; content: Record<string, unknown> }>;\\\\n26\\\\t}\\\\n27\\\\t\\\\n28\\\\texport function readMessageSource(\\\\n29\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n30\\\\t  messageId: string,\\\\n31\\\\t): MessageSource | undefined {\\\\n32\\\\t  const row = db\\\\n33\\\\t    .prepare(`SELECT kind FROM message WHERE message_id = ?`)\\\\n34\\\\t    .get(messageId) as unknown as { kind: string } | undefined;\\\\n35\\\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n36\\\\t  const blocks = db\\\\n37\\\\t    .prepare(\\\\n38\\\\t      `SELECT block_type, content FROM message_block\\\\n39\\\\t       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\\\n40\\\\t    )\\\\n41\\\\t    .all(messageId) as unknown as Array<{ block_type: string; content: string }>;\\\\n42\\\\t  return {\\\\n43\\\\t    messageId,\\\\n44\\\\t    kind: row.kind,\\\\n45\\\\t    blocks: blocks.map((block) => ({\\\\n46\\\\t      blockType: block.block_type,\\\\n47\\\\t      content: JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\\\n48\\\\t    })),\\\\n49\\\\t  };\\\\n50\\\\t}\\\\n51\\\\t\\\\n52\\\\tinterface RawFormRow {\\\\n53\\\\t  subject_id: string;\\\\n54\\\\t  form: string;\\\\n55\\\\t  state: string;\\\\n56\\\\t  content: string | null;\\\\n57\\\\t  reason: string | null;\\\\n58\\\\t  metadata: string | null;\\\\n59\\\\t  source_version: number | bigint;\\\\n60\\\\t  gaps: string | null;\\\\n61\\\\t  derived_at: string | null;\\\\n62\\\\t}\\\\n63\\\\t\\\\n64\\\\t// Every message-owned derived-form row, grouped by message id — the form\\\\n65\\\\t// read-back joined onto message reads (AC-2.1's \\\\\\\"readable alongside the\\\\n66\\\\t// message\\\\\\\"). Rows come back exactly as the queue landed them: state, content,\\\\n67\\\\t// reason, mechanically stamped metadata; nothing is derived at read time.\\\\n68\\\\t//\\\\n69\\\\t// messageIds, when provided, scopes the read to just those subjects so a\\\\n70\\\\t// bounded listMessages loads only its window's forms (AC-3.1's\\\\n71\\\\t// no-load-everything clause), never every message-owned form in the thread.\\\\n72\\\\t// Omitted — the report-surface path that already reads its own scope — reads\\\\n73\\\\t// all message-owned form rows as before.\\\\n74\\\\texport function readMessageForms(\\\\n75\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n76\\\\t  messageIds?: readonly string[],\\\\n77\\\\t): Map<string, DerivedForm[]> {\\\\n78\\\\t  const byMessage = new Map<string, DerivedForm[]>();\\\\n79\\\\t  if (messageIds !== undefined && messageIds.length === 0) return byMessage;\\\\n80\\\\t  const idFilter =\\\\n81\\\\t    messageIds === undefined\\\\n82\\\\t      ? \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n83\\\\t      : ` AND subject_id IN (${messageIds.map(() => \\\\\\\"?\\\\\\\").join(\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\")})`;\\\\n84\\\\t  const rows = db\\\\n85\\\\t    .prepare(\\\\n86\\\\t      `SELECT subject_id, form, state, content, reason, metadata,\\\\n87\\\\t              source_version, gaps, derived_at\\\\n88\\\\t       FROM derived_form WHERE subject_kind = 'message'${idFilter}\\\\n89\\\\t       ORDER BY subject_id, form`,\\\\n90\\\\t    )\\\\n91\\\\t    .all(...(messageIds ?? [])) as unknown as RawFormRow[];\\\\n92\\\\t  for (const row of rows) {\\\\n93\\\\t    const record: DerivedForm = {\\\\n94\\\\t      subjectKind: \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\n95\\\\t      subjectId: row.subject_id,\\\\n96\\\\t      form: row.form as FormKind,\\\\n97\\\\t      state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\\\n98\\\\t      sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\\\n99\\\\t    };\\\\n100\\\\t    if (row.content !== null) record.content = row.content;\\\\n101\\\\t    if (row.reason !== null) record.reason = row.reason;\\\\n102\\\\t    if (row.metadata !== null) {\\\\n103\\\\t      record.metadata = JSON.parse(row.metadata) as DerivedFormMetadata;\\\\n104\\\\t    }\\\\n105\\\\t    if (row.gaps !== null) record.gaps = JSON.parse(row.gaps) as DependencyGap[];\\\\n106\\\\t    if (row.derived_at !== null) record.derivedAt = row.derived_at;\\\\n107\\\\t    const forms = byMessage.get(row.subject_id) ?? [];\\\\n108\\\\t    forms.push(record);\\\\n109\\\\t    byMessage.set(row.subject_id, forms);\\\\n110\\\\t  }\\\\n111\\\\t  return byMessage;\\\\n112\\\\t}\\\\n113\\\\t\\\\n114\\\\t// One form row by exact key — the requeue operation's refusal read (missing\\\\n115\\\\t// row, blocked state, current source version). State returned as stored.\\\\n116\\\\texport function readMessageFormRow(\\\\n117\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n118\\\\t  messageId: string,\\\\n119\\\\t  form: FormKind,\\\\n120\\\\t): { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\\\n121\\\\t  const row = db\\\\n122\\\\t    .prepare(\\\\n123\\\\t      `SELECT state, reason, source_version FROM derived_form\\\\n124\\\\t       WHERE subject_kind = 'message' AND subject_id = ? AND form = ?`,\\\\n125\\\\t    )\\\\n126\\\\t    .get(messageId, form) as unknown as\\\\n127\\\\t    | { state: string; reason: string | null; source_version: number | bigint }\\\\n128\\\\t    | undefined;\\\\n129\\\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n130\\\\t  const view: { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } = {\\\\n131\\\\t    state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\\\n132\\\\t    sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\\\n133\\\\t  };\\\\n134\\\\t  if (row.reason !== null) view.reason = row.reason;\\\\n135\\\\t  return view;\\\\n136\\\\t}\\\\n137\\\\t\\\\n138\\\\t// The message owner's report (Flow 4): one query — message-owned form rows\\\\n139\\\\t// LEFT JOINed with the live work_item still targeting each form at its\\\\n140\\\\t// current source version, if any (DD-1: only live rows exist; terminal\\\\n141\\\\t// outcomes already live on the form). No N+1, no in-memory assembly beyond\\\\n142\\\\t// row mapping. The form→kind CASE is the owner's own queue-site mapping\\\\n143\\\\t// (MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS) inverted.\\\\n144\\\\texport function reportMessageForms(\\\\n145\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n146\\\\t  opts: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string } = {},\\\\n147\\\\t): FormReportEntry[] {\\\\n148\\\\t  const conditions = [\\\\\\\"df.subject_kind = 'message'\\\\\\\"];\\\\n149\\\\t  const params: string[] = [];\\\\n150\\\\t  if (opts.messageId !== undefined) {\\\\n151\\\\t    conditions.push(\\\\\\\"df.subject_id = ?\\\\\\\");\\\\n152\\\\t    params.push(opts.messageId);\\\\n153\\\\t  }\\\\n154\\\\t  // notReady is exact set equality by construction: every state but ready.\\\\n155\\\\t  if (opts.notReady === true) conditions.push(\\\\\\\"df.state <> 'ready'\\\\\\\");\\\\n156\\\\t  const rows = db\\\\n157\\\\t    .prepare(\\\\n158\\\\t      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.form, df.state, df.content, df.reason, df.metadata,\\\\n159\\\\t              df.source_version, df.gaps, df.derived_at,\\\\n160\\\\t              w.status AS queue_status, w.attempts AS queue_attempts,\\\\n161\\\\t              w.last_error AS queue_last_error, w.eligible_at AS queue_eligible_at\\\\n162\\\\t       FROM derived_form df\\\\n163\\\\t       LEFT JOIN work_item w\\\\n164\\\\t         ON w.status IN ('queued', 'claimed')\\\\n165\\\\t        AND w.kind = CASE df.form WHEN 'smoothed_prompt' THEN 'prompt_smoothing' ELSE df.form END\\\\n166\\\\t        AND json_extract(w.source_ref, '$.messageId') = df.subject_id\\\\n167\\\\t        AND COALESCE(json_extract(w.payload, '$.sourceVersion'), 1) = df.source_version\\\\n168\\\\t       WHERE ${conditions.join(\\\\\\\" AND \\\\\\\")}\\\\n169\\\\t       ORDER BY df.subject_id, df.form`,\\\\n170\\\\t    )\\\\n171\\\\t    .all(...params) as unknown as RawReportRow[];\\\\n172\\\\t  return rows.map((row) => reportEntryFromRow(\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\", row));\\\\n173\\\\t}\\\\n174\\\\t\\\\n175\\\\t// The call-id pairing reads. Earliest-recorded block wins if a call id were\\\\n176\\\\t// ever repeated; in a well-formed record the pair is unique. Deleted messages\\\\n177\\\\t// are excluded (tech-design §Mechanics' deleted-read rule, epic-fix-001):\\\\n178\\\\t// composition inputs and derivation reads never see deleted records, so a\\\\n179\\\\t// tool_call whose paired result has been deleted reads no pair and derives\\\\n180\\\\t// outcome `unknown` — never the dead result's outcome.\\\\n181\\\\tfunction findPairedBlock(\\\\n182\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n183\\\\t  blockType: \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\",\\\\n184\\\\t  toolCallId: string,\\\\n185\\\\t): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\\\\n186\\\\t  const row = db\\\\n187\\\\t    .prepare(\\\\n188\\\\t      `SELECT b.content FROM message_block b\\\\n189\\\\t       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\\\n190\\\\t       WHERE b.block_type = ? AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\\\n191\\\\t       ORDER BY m.source_event_order LIMIT 1`,\\\\n192\\\\t    )\\\\n193\\\\t    .get(blockType, toolCallId) as unknown as { content: string } | undefined;\\\\n194\\\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n195\\\\t  return JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>;\\\\n196\\\\t}\\\\n197\\\\t\\\\n198\\\\texport function findPairedToolResult(\\\\n199\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n200\\\\t  toolCallId: string,\\\\n201\\\\t): { content: string; isError: boolean } | undefined {\\\\n202\\\\t  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", toolCallId);\\\\n203\\\\t  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n204\\\\t  return {\\\\n205\\\\t    content: typeof block[\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\"] === \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\" ? block[\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\"] : \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n206\\\\t    isError: block[\\\\\\\"isError\\\\\\\"] === true,\\\\n207\\\\t  };\\\\n208\\\\t}\\\\n209\\\\t\\\\n210\\\\texport function findPairedToolCall(\\\\n211\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n212\\\\t  toolCallId: string,\\\\n213\\\\t): { toolName: string } | undefined {\\\\n214\\\\t  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", toolCallId);\\\\n215\\\\t  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n216\\\\t  return { toolName: typeof block[\\\\\\\"toolName\\\\\\\"] === \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\" ? block[\\\\\\\"toolName\\\\\\\"] : \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" };\\\\n217\\\\t}\\\\n218\\\\t\\\\n219\\\\t// AC-2.8's intake-time lookup: does the paired call's summary sit landed with\\\\n220\\\\t// outcome \\\\\\\"unknown\\\\\\\"? Pending rows carry NULL metadata and never match, so the\\\\n221\\\\t// common case — call and result in one batch, summary not yet run — never\\\\n222\\\\t// triggers a requeue. Returns the call's message id and the form's current\\\\n223\\\\t// source version (the requeue enqueues at version + 1: the pair is the\\\\n224\\\\t// summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate).\\\\n225\\\\texport function findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(\\\\n226\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n227\\\\t  toolCallId: string,\\\\n228\\\\t): { messageId: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\\\n229\\\\t  const row = db\\\\n230\\\\t    .prepare(\\\\n231\\\\t      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.source_version FROM message_block b\\\\n232\\\\t       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\\\n233\\\\t       JOIN derived_form df ON df.subject_kind = 'message'\\\\n234\\\\t         AND df.subject_id = b.message_id AND df.form = 'tool_call_summary'\\\\n235\\\\t       WHERE b.block_type = 'tool_call' AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\\\n236\\\\t         AND json_extract(df.metadata, '$.outcome') = 'unknown'\\\\n237\\\\t       LIMIT 1`,\\\\n238\\\\t    )\\\\n239\\\\t    .get(toolCallId) as unknown as\\\\n240\\\\t    | { subject_id: string; source_version: number | bigint }\\\\n241\\\\t    | undefined;\\\\n242\\\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n243\\\\t  return { messageId: row.subject_id, sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version) };\\\\n244\\\\t}\\\\n245\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"94e40dd3-470d-4837-a704-e0b58191f5b1\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T13:24:35.245Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"// Message-domain reads for derivation (Flow 2): the handler's view of its\\\\n// source message and the call-id pairing reads — the only reach a\\\\n// message-level handler has beyond its own message (AC-2.5). Also the\\\\n// late-result repair lookup intake's projection step runs (AC-2.8): one\\\\n// indexed query by call id, never a scan (the v5 expression index on\\\\n// message_block covers it) and never a drain-time sweep or read-time join.\\\\n// Completion writes for message forms ride the work-queue util's `complete`\\\\n// (Story 1): UPDATE-only with the source-version check — no write path here.\\\\n// Read-back of message-owned form rows (the listMessages join) also lives\\\\n// here: stored state returned as stored — never re-derived on read.\\\\nimport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\\\\\"node:sqlite\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport type {\\\\n  DependencyGap,\\\\n  DerivedForm,\\\\n  DerivedFormMetadata,\\\\n  DerivedFormState,\\\\n  FormKind,\\\\n  FormReportEntry,\\\\n} from \\\\\\\"../../../shared/derivation.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { reportEntryFromRow, type RawReportRow } from \\\\\\\"../../../shared/report.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\nexport interface MessageSource {\\\\n  messageId: string;\\\\n  kind: string;\\\\n  blocks: Array<{ blockType: string; content: Record<string, unknown> }>;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport function readMessageSource(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  messageId: string,\\\\n): MessageSource | undefined {\\\\n  const row = db\\\\n    .prepare(`SELECT kind FROM message WHERE message_id = ?`)\\\\n    .get(messageId) as unknown as { kind: string } | undefined;\\\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n  const blocks = db\\\\n    .prepare(\\\\n      `SELECT block_type, content FROM message_block\\\\n       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\\\n    )\\\\n    .all(messageId) as unknown as Array<{ block_type: string; content: string }>;\\\\n  return {\\\\n    messageId,\\\\n    kind: row.kind,\\\\n    blocks: blocks.map((block) => ({\\\\n      blockType: block.block_type,\\\\n      content: JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\\\n    })),\\\\n  };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\ninterface RawFormRow {\\\\n  subject_id: string;\\\\n  form: string;\\\\n  state: string;\\\\n  content: string | null;\\\\n  reason: string | null;\\\\n  metadata: string | null;\\\\n  source_version: number | bigint;\\\\n  gaps: string | null;\\\\n  derived_at: string | null;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// Every message-owned derived-form row, grouped by message id — the form\\\\n// read-back joined onto message reads (AC-2.1's \\\\\\\"readable alongside the\\\\n// message\\\\\\\"). Rows come back exactly as the queue landed them: state, content,\\\\n// reason, mechanically stamped metadata; nothing is derived at read time.\\\\n//\\\\n// messageIds, when provided, scopes the read to just those subjects so a\\\\n// bounded listMessages loads only its window's forms (AC-3.1's\\\\n// no-load-everything clause), never every message-owned form in the thread.\\\\n// Omitted — the report-surface path that already reads its own scope — reads\\\\n// all message-owned form rows as before.\\\\nexport function readMessageForms(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  messageIds?: readonly string[],\\\\n): Map<string, DerivedForm[]> {\\\\n  const byMessage = new Map<string, DerivedForm[]>();\\\\n  if (messageIds !== undefined && messageIds.length === 0) return byMessage;\\\\n  const idFilter =\\\\n    messageIds === undefined\\\\n      ? \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n      : ` AND subject_id IN (${messageIds.map(() => \\\\\\\"?\\\\\\\").join(\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\")})`;\\\\n  const rows = db\\\\n    .prepare(\\\\n      `SELECT subject_id, form, state, content, reason, metadata,\\\\n              source_version, gaps, derived_at\\\\n       FROM derived_form WHERE subject_kind = 'message'${idFilter}\\\\n       ORDER BY subject_id, form`,\\\\n    )\\\\n    .all(...(messageIds ?? [])) as unknown as RawFormRow[];\\\\n  for (const row of rows) {\\\\n    const record: DerivedForm = {\\\\n      subjectKind: \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\n      subjectId: row.subject_id,\\\\n      form: row.form as FormKind,\\\\n      state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\\\n      sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\\\n    };\\\\n    if (row.content !== null) record.content = row.content;\\\\n    if (row.reason !== null) record.reason = row.reason;\\\\n    if (row.metadata !== null) {\\\\n      record.metadata = JSON.parse(row.metadata) as DerivedFormMetadata;\\\\n    }\\\\n    if (row.gaps !== null) record.gaps = JSON.parse(row.gaps) as DependencyGap[];\\\\n    if (row.derived_at !== null) record.derivedAt = row.derived_at;\\\\n    const forms = byMessage.get(row.subject_id) ?? [];\\\\n    forms.push(record);\\\\n    byMessage.set(row.subject_id, forms);\\\\n  }\\\\n  return byMessage;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// One form row by exact key — the requeue operation's refusal read (missing\\\\n// row, blocked state, current source version). State returned as stored.\\\\nexport function readMessageFormRow(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  messageId: string,\\\\n  form: FormKind,\\\\n): { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\\\n  const row = db\\\\n    .prepare(\\\\n      `SELECT state, reason, source_version FROM derived_form\\\\n       WHERE subject_kind = 'message' AND subject_id = ? AND form = ?`,\\\\n    )\\\\n    .get(messageId, form) as unknown as\\\\n    | { state: string; reason: string | null; source_version: number | bigint }\\\\n    | undefined;\\\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n  const view: { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } = {\\\\n    state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\\\n    sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\\\n  };\\\\n  if (row.reason !== null) view.reason = row.reason;\\\\n  return view;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// The message owner's report (Flow 4): one query — message-owned form rows\\\\n// LEFT JOINed with the live work_item still targeting each form at its\\\\n// current source version, if any (DD-1: only live rows exist; terminal\\\\n// outcomes already live on the form). No N+1, no in-memory assembly beyond\\\\n// row mapping. The form→kind CASE is the owner's own queue-site mapping\\\\n// (MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS) inverted.\\\\nexport function reportMessageForms(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  opts: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string } = {},\\\\n): FormReportEntry[] {\\\\n  const conditions = [\\\\\\\"df.subject_kind = 'message'\\\\\\\"];\\\\n  const params: string[] = [];\\\\n  if (opts.messageId !== undefined) {\\\\n    conditions.push(\\\\\\\"df.subject_id = ?\\\\\\\");\\\\n    params.push(opts.messageId);\\\\n  }\\\\n  // notReady is exact set equality by construction: every state but ready.\\\\n  if (opts.notReady === true) conditions.push(\\\\\\\"df.state <> 'ready'\\\\\\\");\\\\n  const rows = db\\\\n    .prepare(\\\\n      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.form, df.state, df.content, df.reason, df.metadata,\\\\n              df.source_version, df.gaps, df.derived_at,\\\\n              w.status AS queue_status, w.attempts AS queue_attempts,\\\\n              w.last_error AS queue_last_error, w.eligible_at AS queue_eligible_at\\\\n       FROM derived_form df\\\\n       LEFT JOIN work_item w\\\\n         ON w.status IN ('queued', 'claimed')\\\\n        AND w.kind = CASE df.form WHEN 'smoothed_prompt' THEN 'prompt_smoothing' ELSE df.form END\\\\n        AND json_extract(w.source_ref, '$.messageId') = df.subject_id\\\\n        AND COALESCE(json_extract(w.payload, '$.sourceVersion'), 1) = df.source_version\\\\n       WHERE ${conditions.join(\\\\\\\" AND \\\\\\\")}\\\\n       ORDER BY df.subject_id, df.form`,\\\\n    )\\\\n    .all(...params) as unknown as RawReportRow[];\\\\n  return rows.map((row) => reportEntryFromRow(\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\", row));\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// The call-id pairing reads. Earliest-recorded block wins if a call id were\\\\n// ever repeated; in a well-formed record the pair is unique. Deleted messages\\\\n// are excluded (tech-design §Mechanics' deleted-read rule, epic-fix-001):\\\\n// composition inputs and derivation reads never see deleted records, so a\\\\n// tool_call whose paired result has been deleted reads no pair and derives\\\\n// outcome `unknown` — never the dead result's outcome.\\\\nfunction findPairedBlock(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  blockType: \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\",\\\\n  toolCallId: string,\\\\n): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\\\\n  const row = db\\\\n    .prepare(\\\\n      `SELECT b.content FROM message_block b\\\\n       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\\\n       WHERE b.block_type = ? AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\\\n       ORDER BY m.source_event_order LIMIT 1`,\\\\n    )\\\\n    .get(blockType, toolCallId) as unknown as { content: string } | undefined;\\\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n  return JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport function findPairedToolResult(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  toolCallId: string,\\\\n): { content: string; isError: boolean } | undefined {\\\\n  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\", toolCallId);\\\\n  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n  return {\\\\n    content: typeof block[\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\"] === \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\" ? block[\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\"] : \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n    isError: block[\\\\\\\"isError\\\\\\\"] === true,\\\\n  };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport function findPairedToolCall(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  toolCallId: string,\\\\n): { toolName: string } | undefined {\\\\n  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\", toolCallId);\\\\n  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n  return { toolName: typeof block[\\\\\\\"toolName\\\\\\\"] === \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\" ? block[\\\\\\\"toolName\\\\\\\"] : \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// AC-2.8's intake-time lookup: does the paired call's summary sit landed with\\\\n// outcome \\\\\\\"unknown\\\\\\\"? Pending rows carry NULL metadata and never match, so the\\\\n// common case — call and result in one batch, summary not yet run — never\\\\n// triggers a requeue. Returns the call's message id and the form's current\\\\n// source version (the requeue enqueues at version + 1: the pair is the\\\\n// summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate).\\\\nexport function findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(\\\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\\\n  toolCallId: string,\\\\n): { messageId: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\\\n  const row = db\\\\n    .prepare(\\\\n      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.source_version FROM message_block b\\\\n       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\\\n       JOIN derived_form df ON df.subject_kind = 'message'\\\\n         AND df.subject_id = b.message_id AND df.form = 'tool_call_summary'\\\\n       WHERE b.block_type = 'tool_call' AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\\\n         AND json_extract(df.metadata, '$.outcome') = 'unknown'\\\\n       LIMIT 1`,\\\\n    )\\\\n    .get(toolCallId) as unknown as\\\\n    | { subject_id: string; source_version: number | bigint }\\\\n    | undefined;\\\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\\\n  return { messageId: row.subject_id, sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version) };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":245,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":245}}}\\n194:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"content_block_delta\\\",\\\"index\\\":1,\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_delta\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The code already appears to implement the fixes. Let me run the relevant tests to see the actual current state — both the default-\\\"}},\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"d1635a6e-cf61-46fa-8a2c-a43e2c9535ca\\\"}\\n196:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-4-8\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_016iyvcfGBd1aupwooJhYC4c\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The code already appears to implement the fixes. Let me run the relevant tests to see the actual current state — both the default-suite message read test and the process suite.\\\"}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":6265,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":65584,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":6265},\\\"output_tokens\\\":2,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"not_available\\\"},\\\"diagnostics\\\":{\\\"cache_miss_reason\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"unavailable\\\"}},\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"e2b448d4-d9ac-4600-8d3b-e9bf30ee936c\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CbyST78Bkhs3rLhdg1PrA\\\"}\\n204:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"con